lishing"],"released":"Aug 19, 2014","meta":73,"langs":["English","Russian","Polish","German"],"min":[["OS","Windows XP (SP3 required), Vista, 7, 8"],["Processor","2.6 GHz and better"],["Memory","1 GB RAM"],["Graphics","nVidia GeForce 6600 with 128 Mb VRAM or similar AMD card"],["DirectX","Version 9.0c"],["Storage","8 GB available space"],["Sound Card","DirectX 9.0c compliant"]],"rec":[],"deck":2,"blurb":"Villains take the lead in this standalone King's Bounty entry, which turns the usual fantasy setup on its head. You choose from three dark heroes, a demoness, a vampire lord or an orc warlord, each with its own opening situation, individual story and way of playing.\n\nThe world is large and hostile, with towns, wilderness and dungeons full of quests and secrets, and the familiar forces of light stand against you. You build an army and settle fights in turn-based battle, often facing morally dark choices along the way. It suits single-player fans of fantasy tactics who would like to play the other side."}}